{
  "name": "Faculty to chair national scientific committee",
  "parent_id": 203314454715942,
  "group_id": "97cdccc4-fc56-4595-9ef4-c7c3b606b1f6",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-30T15:22:13.239Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-07-30T15:22:13.313Z",
  "published_at": "2026-07-30T15:22:13.300Z",
  "id": 203715924979037,
  "uuid": "2c029979-d466-412f-a53f-f30bdd177200",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "dcdb9385-38d8-51ab-6997-46f3d9d4047f",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "71b427f8-a572-4ab7-af0b-5860166ee27d",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The associate professor at AKU, who is also a renowned\ncardiothoracic surgeon, will lead efforts to raise awareness about the science\nbehind cardiovascular diseases (CVD) - a prominent public health problem in\nPakistan. During his term, Dr Sharif and his team will highlight the poor\nlifestyle habits that cause CVD and also work to make treatment more accessible\nfor those with advanced cardiac conditions.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"While heart disease is common; it can be avoided,\"\nsaid Dr Sharif. \"A healthy diet and regular exercise are essential preventive\nmeasures and we need to strive to ensure that everyone has the knowledge to take\ncharge of their health.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The scientific council will also develop a set of\ncomprehensive quality indicators alongside professional regulations to help new\ncardiac facilities raise their quality of care. Such measures will ensure that\nlife-saving surgeries are available outside of renowned private institutions\nand busy public hospitals which are unable to cope with the rising burden of\nCVDs.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Patients often opt for treatment at smaller and\nsometimes unqualified healthcare centers on cost grounds. Regardless of where\nthey go, patients must always receive the right guidance so that they opt for\nthe most suitable and beneficial treatment,\" said Dr Sharif who trained in\nsurgery as a Rhodes scholar at the University of Oxford and Harvard University\nprior to joining AKU in August 2000.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Another priority for Dr Sharif is the need to improve\nthe professional rapport between cardiologists and cardiac surgeons.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"There are approximately 50 cardiologists for every\ncardiac surgeon in Pakistan. There needs to be a strong working relationship\nbetween these two sets of specialists as this will immediately result in a\nbetter experience for patients.\" ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The Pakistan Cardiac Society is a\nnational body founded in 1966 which is focused on promoting research and\ntreatment advances in cardiovascular disease.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
